file tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish -- ten behaviors asserted BY NAME, since a named case reds when deleted where a total only shrinks
file construction/REDS.md -- booked and CLOSED as `%530`; booked `%529` from a spine reading shared_max=528, and the rebase found a peer had bound that number to an earlier stamp, so the row renumbered and the STAMP is what every citation of it already spelled
file construction/archive/REDS-a-record-that-parted-from-the-act-rows-523.md -- the shelf %523 folded to, which bought the ledger pin the room this lap's row needed; written for %518 beside it and rewritten for one row when the rebase showed a peer had folded %518 an hour earlier
